  "label": "User projected onto the textual message implying personal interaction",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'okay now make sure to get my good side' which uses the first-person plural 'my' to imply the user is the one who must 'get' Hitler's 'good side'. This creates a direct address to the viewer, making the user feel personally involved in the absurd and hateful scenario. The projection is onto the textual material, which frames the user as the recipient of Hitler's supposed 'good side' offer.",
